old release client hash=C31D6B7E4DD38F8FE7EDBBEE707A7636A6740AA5F3893175191DAB34FC0C98F0
```

Important limitation discovered on the physical target: v0.1.20 predates the updater and contains no `wifimic_client_updater.exe`. The released v0.2.0 updater embeds `WIFIMIC_CLIENT_VERSION=v0.2.0`, so after the required v0.2.0 bootstrap it reports NoOp even if the client bytes are manually replaced by v0.1.20. To reach the update path without inventing a release asset, a temporary updater fixture was built from the tagged v0.2.0 source with only the compile-time version environment set to `v0.1.20`:

```text
source=tagged v0.2.0 source
fixture embedded WIFIMIC_CLIENT_VERSION=v0.1.20
fixture updater hash=7182165144247BAD2103C6A08802721C737707C08234020987E94856D7AE1F3F
```

This fixture was copied temporarily to the installed updater path; it is explicitly not claimed to be the published v0.2.0 updater artifact.

The old client bytes and fixture updater were installed at the canonical paths after the task was Ready and no client process was running. The real updater was then invoked with empty stdin so its real console wait could complete:

```text
installed updater path=C:\Program Files\wifimic-client\wifimic_client_updater.exe
invocation=empty-stdin | installed updater path
檢查中...
更新失敗：更新失敗且無法確認還原狀態
請按 Enter 鍵結束...
updater_exit=1
```

Post-failure state showed the real rollback defect:

```text
