```

For the second real invocation, the v0.1.20 client and the tagged-source `v0.1.20` fixture updater were installed temporarily. A unique outbound Windows Firewall rule blocked TCP/443 only for the updater executable:

```text
New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName 'F3 temporary updater network interruption' -Direction Outbound -Action Block -Program <installed updater> -Protocol TCP -RemotePort 443
temporary_rule_added=True
```

The rule was removed in a `finally` cleanup block regardless of updater result. The real updater run produced:

```text
檢查中...
更新失敗：GitHub release request failed: io: 嘗試存取通訊端被拒絕，因為存取權限不足。 (os error 10013)
請按 Enter 鍵結束...
network_failure_updater_exit=1
temporary_rule_after_remove=0
```

This was a controlled pre-download/release-resolution network failure, not a fabricated mid-download event. Because the updater downloads before task/executable mutation, the result proves the no-mutation preflight failure path, not automatic post-mutation rollback. After cleanup/restoration:

```text
